              "raw": "{\n  \"companyName\": \"\",\n  \"industryId\": 18,\n  \"companyTypeId\": 1,\n  \"companySize\": null,\n  \"annualRevenue\": null,\n  \"website\": \"\",\n  \"phone\": \"9845012345\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "text"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/company",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "company"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Corresponds to: clicking 'Next' without entering a Company Name -> mandatory field validation error for 'Company Name', form not submitted.\n\nNOTE: I haven't seen this API's actual validation-error response shape yet (only the success response was captured). Submit this request once in Postman, check the real error JSON structure, and tighten the 'Validation error' test above to check the exact field/message path instead of a generic string search."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
